      "caption": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Rune gestated by Fia, the Deathbed Companion.\nUsed to restore the fractured Elden Ring when brandished by the Elden Lord.\n\nFormed of the two hallowbrand half-wheels combined, it will embed the principle of life within Death into Order. \n\nThe Golden Order was created by confining Destined Death. Thus, this new Order will be one of Death restored.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Caption"
        }
      },
      "description": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Can be used to mend the shattered Elden Ring",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Description"
        }
      },
      "location": {
        "known": true,
        "value": "Obtaining this item, like the other mending runes, will not affect any other ending.; It should be noted that death has always existed in the Lands Between, noted by the various enemies the player slays and the myriad deaths they incur before being brought back through the guidance of grace.; Destined Death, or the Rune of Death (interchangeable names per Enia dialogue) is unbound after Maliketh's defeat and \" the Lands Between are shrouded by Death's dark fate \" (per Enia dialogue). This happens before all endings.",
        "provenance": {
          "source": "legacy_db_data",
          "method": "copied from legacy ItemTexts.Location"
        }
      },
